{
  "requirement": "The `habeas-evidence` skill MUST tell agents not to write placeholder evidence for a requirement or example whose implementation is pending.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligation.** `requirements.cli.pending_evidence_guidance.no_placeholder` has one MUST. The `habeas-evidence` skill must tell agents not to write placeholder evidence for a requirement or example whose implementation is pending. The requirement is documentation-like, so a test can only check what the bundled skill text says.\n\n**Test.** `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_evidence_skill_never_writes_placeholder_evidence_for_pending_work]` is marked `{test}` for the requirement. It does three things:\n- It finds the workflow step of `habeas-evidence` that contains \"Stop and report each finding that needs the user\", using `step_of`.\n- It takes that step's collapsed text, using `step` and `workflow_steps`.\n- It asserts with `assert_text_in_order` that the step contains \"names only implementation that is still pending\" and, after it, \"never write placeholder evidence\".\n\nThe helpers behave as that needs. `workflow_steps` parses the numbered steps of the skill's Workflow section and collapses whitespace, so phrases that wrap across lines still match. `assert_text_in_order` panics if a phrase is absent or out of order.\n\n**Match to the skill.** Step 5 of `assets/skills/habeas-evidence/SKILL.md` says to report \"a missing record or false judgment whose rationale names only implementation that is still pending, which is expected. Don't keep iterating on those, and never write placeholder evidence.\" The test therefore checks both halves of the obligation: the pending-implementation condition and the prohibition on placeholder evidence. It also checks that they are in the same step, in the right order.\n\n**Gaps.** I found none. The requirement has no other conditions, modes or boundaries. A skill that dropped the prohibition, or that dropped the pending-implementation context, would fail the assertions. No fixme is involved.",
